# Always commit after work

When a task that changes the repo is finished, create a git commit unless the user explicitly says not to.

- Follow the repo's commit message style (concise, why-focused).
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, `*.creds`, Snapcraft credentials, tokens).
- Do not push unless the user asks (or a prior rule/request already covers push for that task).
- If the only leftover is secret/untracked junk, still commit the real code changes and leave secrets untracked.
